# stack/icedrive/icedrive.pin — WHICH IceDrive binaries this image may carry.
#
# TWO ARTIFACTS, TWO PINS, because there are two clients and they are not
# interchangeable:
#
#   APPIMAGE_*  the 118 MB GUI client. Needs a display, so it needs the SR-015
#               graphical session. Its credential is typed into its own GUI over
#               RDP and cannot be handed to it from here. This is the direction
#               the Owner chose on 2026-08-27.
#   CLI_*       the 9.8 MB headless native ELF. No X at all, non-interactive
#               login, FUSE mount. Proven working on the bench box, but it is a
#               MOUNT client and not a SYNC client — see README.md before
#               choosing it.
#
# WHICH ONE RIDES THE USB IS NOT DECIDED HERE. HomeHub's config.homehub.psd1
# `Extras.IceDrive` picks `off` / `appimage` / `cli`, and that one declaration
# drives both the carriage (which artifact export-icedrive.sh stages) and the
# activation (ICEDRIVE_MODE in .env). A pin with no matching Extras entry is
# simply unused; an Extras entry with no matching pin is REFUSED by
# Materialize-Deploy, because activation without carriage is an instruction
# nobody can follow.
#
# NEITHER BINARY IS IN THIS REPO AND NEITHER IS FETCHED BY THE BUILD.
# icedrive.net is behind Cloudflare and answers 403 to anything that is not a
# browser — including for the CLI installer, so the widely-quoted
#     curl -s https://icedrive.net/download/linux/cli/install.sh | bash
# PIPES AN HTML CHALLENGE PAGE INTO BASH. Do not use it. Each file is supplied
# once by the operator, verified against the SHA256 below, and cached, so every
# build after that is reproducible and needs no vendor at all.
#
# WHY NOT COMMIT THEM: ~118 MB of git history per version bump, forever, for
# vendor artifacts this project does not own.
#
# HOW TO SET OR BUMP EITHER:
#   1. Download it from icedrive.net in a browser.
#   2. bash vmtest/export-icedrive.sh --print-hash --from ~/Downloads/<file>
#   3. Put the version and that hash below, in the matching pair.
#   4. bash vmtest/export-icedrive.sh --out vmtest/.out/icedrive \
#          --artifact appimage --from ~/Downloads/<file>
#      It verifies, caches and stages it. Later builds reuse the cache.
#
# AN UNSET PAIR IS A VALID, SHIPPED STATE: that artifact is simply not carried.
# Both unset is this repo's default posture — the deployer ships IceDrive OFF.
#
# FORMAT: KEY=VALUE, one per line. `#` starts a comment. Blank lines ignored.

# ── the GUI client (Icedrive Mount & Sync, AppImage) ────────────────────────
# Version strings are informational; the SHA256 is the identity.
APPIMAGE_VERSION=3.62
APPIMAGE_SHA256=091d7ec7fab8e230f4714558b4a5953cddb7d418144b3b0c869a002e0c496194

# ── the headless CLI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CLI_VERSION=3.62
CLI_SHA256=341eccb27046452bcfc63a081d605a933e583a3db4757e8c98647921d0cb68b3

# Optional, per artifact. If the vendor ever serves a direct, non-Cloudflared
# URL, put it here and export-icedrive.sh will try it before asking for --from.
# Left empty because no such URL exists today (see the 403 note above).
APPIMAGE_URL=
CLI_URL=
